class ProjectLayoutPage {
  +workspaceId: Signal<Guid>
  +canChangeMode: Signal<boolean>
  +revision: Signal<number>
  +draft: Signal<DraftState>
  +workspace: Signal<WorkspaceDetail | null>
  +openDialog(kind: WorkspaceActionKind): void
  +refresh(): void
  +modeChanged(): void
}
note right of ProjectLayoutPage
  canChangeMode = workspaces.changeMode in
  currentSession.capabilities. openDialog uses the
  workspace the header last resolved (workspaceLoaded);
  before that a request does nothing. modeChanged():
  revision + 1 reloads the header and the active
  tab; re-navigating the current tab URL lets
  BoardModeGuard re-match the board. A resolved
  header without a Sprints tab while the child route
  is sprints navigates to overview (replaceUrl).
  While one of its dialogs is open, revision still
  increments at once, but the re-navigation and the
  sprints redirect wait until the dialog closes
  (deactivating the child page would dismiss it).
  Dialog close result (toasts via TOAST_SERVICE):
  Changed -> modeChanged() + "Now using" toast;
  Outdated -> modeChanged(); once the reloaded
  header resolves, the "project changed" info
  toast, or, after a relayed unconfirmed, the
  neutral "Community Hackathon 2026 uses Kanban
  now." naming the mode it shows (after a 404 the
  read fails: only the tab's not-found);
  CloseSprint(sprint) -> CloseSprintDialog with
  sprint.sprintId and offerSprintsLink (false only
  on the sprints tab; scrum close-sprint); no result
  -> nothing.
  unconfirmed (dialog still open) -> modeChanged():
  revision + 1 at once; the dialog stays open and
  the re-navigation waits for its close.
  CloseSprintOutcome: Closed -> refresh() +
  "Sprint 8 closed" toast with its counts;
  Outdated -> refresh(). Still open: unconfirmed
  -> refresh(); forbidden -> "Your access
  changed" toast, no Retry.
  Implements FormDraft by delegating to its dialog;
  every child page's draft falls back to it.
end note
